      "content": "I understand your frustration, and I apologize for the earlier distraction. Here is the direct, technical diagnostic checklist you need for your GKE CrashLoopBackOff issue:\n\n1.  **Check for OOMKilled:**\n    *   Run `kubectl describe pod <pod-name>` and look at the `Events` section at the bottom.\n    *   Search for `OOMKilled`. If present, the container was killed by the OS due to memory pressure, not a probe failure.\n    *   Check `kubectl get events` to see the specific reason for the restart.\n\n2.  **Verify Probe Configuration:**\n    *   Inspect your Deployment YAML (or `kubectl get deployment <name> -o yaml`).\n    *   Ensure `initialDelaySeconds` is sufficient (e.g., 10-30s) so the app has time to start before the probe hits.\n    *   Confirm the `port` in the probe matches the actual port your service listens on (e.g., 8080).\n    *   Check if `failureThreshold` is too low, causing a restart before the app is ready.\n\n3.  **Analyze Application Logs:**",
